# Rank 1740 / CVE-2022-23837: Sidekiq's Web UI dashboard passed the `days`
# query parameter straight into the stats-history window. `params["days"]` is
# request input, and Ruby's `to_i` never raises -- `"1000000"` coerces to a
# million, garbage to 0 -- so `Sidekiq::Stats::History.new((params["days"] ||
# 30).to_i)` handed the peer an unbounded window count, and `date_stat_hash`
# iterated `@start_date.downto(@start_date - @days_previous + 1)`, building a
# date-keyed array and one Redis MGET of that size per request (CWE-400 DoS in
# the Web UI). Fix 7785ac13 bounds the window twice: the route validates
# `days < 1 || days > 180` and halts 401, and `History#initialize` raises
# ArgumentError outside 1..(5*365). The parent 0a4de94 is vulnerable and the
# remediation is present at the fixed revision, so the row is sound.
#
# ATTENTION, rechecked. Both blockers stand, measured against the real
# checkout at 0a4de94 and 7785ac1, three --cache off runs per side, and the
# construct isolated with the shipped `eval` sink so the legs stay testable
# without a throwaway binding.
#
# 1. Both revisions report identically: 65 findings and 8 review flags each,
#    nothing on web/application.rb:50-56 or api.rb:161-190 in either. The
#    flags all sit in the JavaScript dashboard assets and the test suite.
#    `vyql trace -from HttpInput` over lib/sidekiq finds 4 reachable
#    source-to-sink pairs (all csrf_protection.rb into web/action.rb:45) and
#    79 dead-end sources; the dashboard route's read is among the dead ends.
# 2. The count never crosses the constructor. `params` and
#    `params.__subscript` are labelled code.HttpInput at
#    web/application.rb:53 and the taint survives `.to_i` and the `|| 30`
#    default, but a constructor argument never enters the resolved
#    `initialize` body at all: `H.new(params["q"])` with
#    `def initialize(x); eval(x)` reports nothing while the identical value
#    through a plain method parameter (`f.use(params["q"])` with
#    `def use(x); eval(x)`) reports VYQL-INJ-003 critical, and `H.new` itself
#    resolves -- it is absent from the unresolved-callee list. The member
#    below pins that leg alone.
# 3. An instance variable written in one method never flows to a read in
#    another: `@x = x` in `initialize` then `eval(@x)` in a sibling method
#    reports nothing even in a single file. That is the Ruby instance of the
#    aliasReceiverSelf field-crossing family, and it sits behind leg 2, so
#    both relations have to land before the real two-file member can report.
#    Neither is a localized correction -- constructor-argument-to-body and
#    field-write-to-reader are new dataflow relations -- so the engine-gap
#    entry stands.
# 4. No iteration-count sink exists in any language, so even a fully resolved
#    path has nothing to fire on. A presence route does not substitute: a
#    class-scope binding on `call in ["downto","upto"]` matches fifteen
#    class contexts in api.rb alone, because a class context carries every
#    nested class's body; adding `containsAny(expr,["@"])` narrows none of
#    them (15 -> 15), and adding `not (call in ["raise"])` suppresses all
#    fifteen (15 -> 0), because any `raise` anywhere in the nesting silences
#    the class. Measured on both revisions: 65 = 65 findings, zero effect.
#    The route-side form is no better -- `params[...]` subscripted and
#    coerced appears on 178 lines in 116 Ruby files across the corpus
#    clones, the pagination and validation idiom, and none of them carries a
#    halt. Same measured-unshippable family as 1517, 1534, 1554, 1559, 1572,
#    1586 and 1612.
#
# Members 1 and 2 pin the real two-file shape against VYQL-DOS-042, the rule
# of the right weakness class that exists today. Members 3 to 5 isolate the
# legs with the shipped eval sink: member 3 is the control that reports
# today, member 4 must flip when constructor-argument taint enters the
# resolved initialize body, member 5 when the instance-variable hop lands.
# The patched member must stay reject under all of them.

test "rank1740: the dashboard passes the unvalidated days parameter straight into the stats history window"
  lang ruby
  file sidekiq/web/application.rb
  reject VYQL-DOS-042
  code
  ```
  module Sidekiq
    class WebApplication
      get "/" do
        @redis_info = redis_info.select { |k, v| REDIS_KEYS.include? k }
        stats_history = Sidekiq::Stats::History.new((params["days"] || 30).to_i)
        @processed_history = stats_history.processed
        @failed_history = stats_history.failed

        erb(:dashboard)
      end
    end
  end
  ```
  file sidekiq/api.rb
  code
  ```
  module Sidekiq
    module Stats
      class History
        def initialize(days_previous, start_date = nil)
          @days_previous = days_previous
          @start_date = start_date || Time.now.utc.to_date
        end

        def processed
          @processed ||= date_stat_hash("processed")
        end

        def failed
          @failed ||= date_stat_hash("failed")
        end

        private

        def date_stat_hash(stat)
          stat_hash = {}
          dates = @start_date.downto(@start_date - @days_previous + 1).map { |date|
            date.strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
          }

          keys = dates.map { |datestr| "stat:#{stat}:#{datestr}" }

          Sidekiq.redis do |conn|
            conn.mget(keys).each_with_index do |value, idx|
              stat_hash[dates[idx]] = value ? value.to_i : 0
            end
          end

          stat_hash
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1740: the fixed revision bounds the window at the route and raises in the constructor"
  lang ruby
  file sidekiq/web/application.rb
  reject VYQL-DOS-042
  code
  ```
  module Sidekiq
    class WebApplication
      get "/" do
        @redis_info = redis_info.select { |k, v| REDIS_KEYS.include? k }
        days = (params["days"] || 30).to_i
        return halt(401) if days < 1 || days > 180

        stats_history = Sidekiq::Stats::History.new(days)
        @processed_history = stats_history.processed
        @failed_history = stats_history.failed

        erb(:dashboard)
      end
    end
  end
  ```
  file sidekiq/api.rb
  code
  ```
  module Sidekiq
    module Stats
      class History
        def initialize(days_previous, start_date = nil)
          # we only store five years of data in Redis
          raise ArgumentError if days_previous < 1 || days_previous > (5 * 365)
          @days_previous = days_previous
          @start_date = start_date || Time.now.utc.to_date
        end

        def processed
          @processed ||= date_stat_hash("processed")
        end

        def failed
          @failed ||= date_stat_hash("failed")
        end

        private

        def date_stat_hash(stat)
          stat_hash = {}
          dates = @start_date.downto(@start_date - @days_previous + 1).map { |date|
            date.strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
          }

          keys = dates.map { |datestr| "stat:#{stat}:#{datestr}" }

          Sidekiq.redis do |conn|
            conn.mget(keys).each_with_index do |value, idx|
              stat_hash[dates[idx]] = value ? value.to_i : 0
            end
          end

          stat_hash
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1740: the same count through a plain method parameter reaches the consumer"
  lang ruby
  file sidekiq/web/application.rb
  expect VYQL-INJ-003
  code
  ```
  module Sidekiq
    module Stats
      class History
        def initialize(start_date = nil)
          @start_date = start_date || Time.now.utc.to_date
        end

        def keys_for(days_previous)
          dates = @start_date.downto(@start_date - days_previous + 1).map { |date|
            date.strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
          }
          eval(dates.length.to_s)
          dates.map { |datestr| "stat:processed:#{datestr}" }
        end
      end
    end

    class WebApplication
      get "/" do
        days = (params["days"] || 30).to_i
        history = Stats::History.new
        history.keys_for(days)
      end
    end
  end
  ```

